@format 1
@id ui-event.e529dc9caf79c29d
@title Console button click
@section I. UI
@area UI event
@tabs Global interface
@event-ref cs|PMainArea/PConsole.cs|PConsoleButtonBuild|pButton|Click|1
@entry input
@summary Invoke the handler supplied for a console button; Clear Tabs confirms destruction and starts the all-workspace media reset.
@tag click
@tag PConsole
@alias owner = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PConsole
@alias tabset = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.LTabset

[input] Console button clicked <input>
- Invoke the routed click handler supplied when the reusable button was built @ owner.PConsoleButtonBuild
> handler

[handler] Which handler owns this button? <decision>
? "Clear Tabs handler" > confirm
? "Another console action" > other

[confirm] Confirm destructive clearing <decision>
- Ask for confirmation according to the destructive-action preference @ owner.PConsoleTabsHandle
@ owner.PConsoleDestructiveConfirm
? "Declined" > unchanged
? "Confirmed" > clear

[clear] Clear all tab workspaces <process>
- Invoke the tabset's all-workspace content clear @ tabset.LTabsetContentClear
> output

[output] Tabs cleared <output>
= Every tab's media-dependent workspace state is reset without closing the tabs.
! Code binding: cs|PMainArea/PConsole.cs|PConsoleButtonBuild|pButton|Click|1

[other] Delegated console action <output>
= The button-specific handler completes its own operation.

[unchanged] Clearing cancelled <output>
= Tab content remains unchanged.
